From 7c02051b8d95ae253e4272bb82102f7f4b7e4546 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jniedergang <julien.niedergang@suse.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 13:08:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Support the oscap options that select rules and content in
 xccdf_eval (#780)

* Support the oscap options that select rules and content in xccdf_eval

xccdf_eval rebuilds the oscap command line from a fixed set of keyword
arguments, so anything else a caller asks for is dropped without a word.
SUSE Multi-Linux Manager exposes an oscap arguments field that ends up
here, which means a user asking to skip a rule gets a compliance report
where that rule was evaluated anyway.

Add the options that select which rules are evaluated and where the
content comes from: skip_rule, reference, cpe, local_files, datastream_id,
xccdf_id and benchmark_id. rule and skip_rule now accept either a single
string or a list, since oscap accepts those options more than once.

The options that write result files (results, results-arf, report,
stig-viewer, thin-results) are deliberately left out: the caller owns
those paths and already passes them explicitly.
